==Latin==

===Etymology===
From {{m|la|tam}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|tantus}}

===Adjective===
{{la-adj-1&2|tantus|tanta|tantum}}

# of such [[size]]
# so [[much]], so [[great]]

====Inflection====
{{la-decl-1&2|tant}}

====Usage notes====
* Being naturally adjective, ''tantus'' was then used substantively as ''tantum'' (frequently with genitive) to mean ''"so much of"'', ''"so many of"''; as ''tantī (pretiī)'' to mean ''"so high (a price)"''; adverbially as ''tantum'' to mean ''"so much"'', ''"to such degree"'' (cf. {{m|la|tam}}); as ''tantō'' to mean ''"by so much"''. For all these ''quantus'' has its coordinate functions.

====Coordinate terms====
* {{l|la|quantus}}

